.SH "NAME"
systemd-hwdb \- hardware database management tool
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.HP \w'\fBsystemd\-hwdb\ \fR\fB[options]\fR\fB\ update\fR\ 'u
\fBsystemd\-hwdb \fR\fB[options]\fR\fB update\fR
.HP \w'\fBsystemd\-hwdb\ \fR\fB[options]\fR\fB\ query\ \fR\fB\fImodalias\fR\fR\ 'u
\fBsystemd\-hwdb \fR\fB[options]\fR\fB query \fR\fB\fImodalias\fR\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBsystemd\-hwdb\fR
expects a command and command specific arguments\&. It manages the binary hardware database\&.
.PP
eudev provides this command for the scripts and packages that call the command of the same name of systemd\&. It shares the code with
\fBudevadm hwdb\fR, see
\fBudevadm\fR(8), and like that, it writes
hwdb\&.bin
in the format configured with
\fIhwdb_format=\fR
in
\fBudev.conf\fR(5)\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"

\fB\-\-usr\fR
.RS 4
Generate in the udev library directory, e\&.g\&.\&
/usr/lib/udev, instead of
/etc/udev\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-root=\fR\fB\fIPATH\fR\fR
.RS 4
Alternate root path in the filesystem\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-strict\fR
.RS 4
When updating, return non\-zero exit value on any parsing error\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Print a short version string and exit\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Print a short help text and exit\&.
.RE
.SS "systemd\-hwdb [\fIoptions\fR] update"
Update the binary database\&. If no hwdb files are found, the binary database is removed\&. A directory of hwdb files that does not exist is skipped, but if one exists and cannot be read, e\&.g\&. because it is not a directory, or a hwdb file cannot be read, the update fails, and the binary database is kept as it is\&. systemd skips such a directory or file\&.
.SS "systemd\-hwdb [\fIoptions\fR] query \fIMODALIAS\fR"
Query database and print result\&.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"

\fI$SYSTEMD_HWDB_UPDATE_BYPASS\fR
.RS 4
If set to a true value,
\fBsystemd\-hwdb update\fR
does nothing and exits successfully, like in systemd\&.
.RE
.PP
\fI$UDEV_HWDB_PATH\fR
.RS 4
Additional directories of hwdb files, separated by colons, which are read after the system directories, and like them below the root directory given with
\fB\-\-root=\fR, see
\fBhwdb\fR(7)\&. A relative directory is relative to that root directory, or else to the current directory\&.
.RE
.PP
\fI$UDEV_HWDB_BIN\fR
.RS 4
The
hwdb\&.bin
that
\fBsystemd\-hwdb query\fR
reads before the ones of the system, unless
\fB\-\-root=\fR
is given\&.
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBhwdb\fR(7),
\fBudevadm\fR(8),
\fBudev.conf\fR(5)
